# Distributed PyTorch Training on 2 Nodes (Kathara)

This lab runs distributed training on 2 virtual machines connected over a shared collision domain (A), comparing DDP against manual weight synchronization at the end of each epoch.

## 1. Dataset Setup

Place the pre-downloaded FashionMNIST dataset inside:
shared/data/FashionMNIST/raw/

Both machines access this data through the shared folder. DistributedSampler partitions 30,000 samples to each node.

---

## 2. Start the Lab and Wireshark

From the host command prompt:

kathara lstart

Attach Wireshark to collision domain A:

kathara lconfig -n wireshark --add A

Open browser at:
http://localhost:3000

---

## 3. Option A: Run DDP Training (Sync Every Batch)

On pc1 (Rank 0 - Master):
python3 /shared/Train_DDP.py 0

Immediately after, on pc2 (Rank 1):
python3 /shared/Train_DDP.py 1

---

## 4. Option B: Run Manual Sync Training (Sync at Epoch End)

On pc1 (Rank 0 - Master):
python3 /shared/Train_Sync_Manuale.py 0

Immediately after, on pc2 (Rank 1):
python3 /shared/Train_Sync_Manuale.py 1

Both scripts automatically track and print execution time, sent packets, and total transferred MB.

---

## 5. Stop the Lab

When execution finishes, shut down the lab from the host terminal:

kathara lclean
